# Vendored into CrewCode. Upstream's dev workflow clones each package directory
# separately and ignored them all here; in this repo they ARE the tracked source
# for the 14 file: dependencies in the root package.json, so those entries are
# gone. Build output (dist/) stays ignored via the root .gitignore and is
# regenerated by each package's `prepare` script on install.
node_modules
package-lock.json
/demo/demo.js*
/demo/demo.d.ts*
/demo/test/test.js*
/website
.tern-*

# dist/ is ignored repo-wide, but these packages are consumed as `file:` deps
# and npm cannot build them at install time: it runs their `prepare` script in
# the source dir, whose devDependencies were never installed (cm-buildhelper:
# command not found, exit 127). So the built output ships. Regenerate with
# `npm run codemirror:build` and commit the result.
!dist/
